---
const blurConfig = `decoration {
    blur {
        enabled = true
        size = 12
        passes = 4
    }
}`;
---

<section class="section transparency" id="transparency">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="intro reveal">
      <h2 class="h-section">Transparent panels. Blurred wallpaper.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Let the desktop show through without losing your place. Hyprland blurs the wallpaper behind the panels; filenames, icons and previews stay sharp.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="reveal">
      <div class="frame comparison" id="transparency-compare" style="--split:50%">
        <img src="/media/s/transparency-off.webp" alt="HyprFM with opaque panels over a blue and rose landscape wallpaper" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="transparent" src="/media/s/transparency-on.webp" alt="The same HyprFM window with the wallpaper visible and blurred behind its panels" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <span class="divider" aria-hidden="true"><span>↔</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-labels" aria-hidden="true"><span>Opaque</span><span>Transparency + blur</span></div>
      <label for="transparency-slider">Drag to compare <span class="sr-only">opaque on the left and transparent on the right. Use the arrow keys to move the divider.</span></label>
      <input id="transparency-slider" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" aria-controls="transparency-compare" />
      <figcaption>Look at the contour lines: sharp outside the window, blurred behind the files. These are matching real app captures, with native Hyprland blur.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <details class="toggle-demo reveal">
      <summary>Watch the real transparency toggle <span>8 seconds · silent</span></summary>
      <div class="frame recording">
        <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/l/transparency.jpg" aria-label="HyprFM switching between opaque and transparent panels using Ctrl+Shift+B">
          <source src="/media/l/transparency.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <p><a href="/media/l/transparency.mp4">Watch the transparency demo.</a></p>
        </video>
      </div>
      <p>The recording toggles blur-backed transparency on, holds, then returns to opaque panels.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="blur-setup reveal">
      <summary>Set up transparency and blur</summary>
      <div class="setup-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>1. Enable transparency in HyprFM</h3>
          <p>Use Settings, press <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+B</kbd>, or edit <code>config.toml</code>.</p>
          <pre><code>[appearance]
transparency_enabled = true</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>2. Enable blur in Hyprland</h3>
          <p>The compositor blurs the backdrop. These are the settings used in this capture.</p>
          <pre><code>{blurConfig}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="setup-note">On KDE Plasma, HyprFM also supports native KWin blur.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const slider = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#transparency-slider')!;
  const comparison = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#transparency-compare')!;
  function updateComparison() {
    comparison.style.setProperty('--split', `${slider.value}%`);
  }
  slider.addEventListener('input', updateComparison);
  function moveDivider(event: PointerEvent) {
    const bounds = comparison.getBoundingClientRect();
    slider.value = String(Math.max(0, Math.min(100, (event.clientX - bounds.left) / bounds.width * 100)));
    updateComparison();
  }
  comparison.addEventListener('pointerdown', (event) => {
    if (!event.isPrimary || event.button !== 0) return;
    comparison.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
    moveDivider(event);
  });
  comparison.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {
    if (comparison.hasPointerCapture(event.pointerId)) moveDivider(event);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .transparency { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mantle) 45%, var(--page)); border-block: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .intro { display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .intro .lede { max-width: 68ch; }
  kbd { color: var(--text); font-size: .85em; white-space: nowrap; }
  figure { margin: 0; }
  .comparison { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; cursor: ew-resize; touch-action: pan-y; }
  .comparison > img { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; user-select: none; }
  .transparent { clip-path: inset(0 0 0 var(--split)); }
  .divider { position: absolute; inset-block: 0; left: var(--split); width: 2px; background: var(--accent); pointer-events: none; }
  .divider > span { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: -19px; width: 40px; height: 40px; display: grid; place-items: center; border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 50%; background: var(--crust); color: var(--text); font-size: 22px; }
  .comparison-labels { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; margin-top: 20px; font: 600 12px/1.5 var(--mono); color: var(--subtext); }
  label { display: block; font-size: 14px; color: var(--subtext); text-align: center; margin-top: 12px; }
  input { display: block; width: 100%; min-height: 44px; margin: 0 0 10px; accent-color: var(--accent); cursor: ew-resize; }
  figcaption, .toggle-demo p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--subtext); }
  .toggle-demo { margin-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  summary { padding-block: 18px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  summary span { display: inline-block; margin-left: 12px; font: 400 12px/1.5 var(--mono); color: var(--subtext); }
  .recording { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; margin: 4px 0 18px; }
  .toggle-demo p { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .blur-setup { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .setup-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; padding: 8px 0 20px; }
  .setup-grid > div { min-width: 0; }
  h3 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .setup-grid p, .setup-note { color: var(--subtext); font-size: 13px; }
  pre { margin: 16px 0 0; padding: 16px; background: var(--crust); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 5px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; }
  .setup-note { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .setup-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { summary span { display: block; margin: 5px 0 0 18px; } }
</style>
